# 3. FUNDAMENTAL DEFINITIONS

Agent:

An engineering worker that performs a specialized engineering responsibility.

Skill:

A reusable engineering capability.

Tool:

A controlled execution capability.

Model:

The reasoning/inference provider used by an Agent.

Graph:

The engineering topology defining what work happens, dependencies, branches, conditions and execution relationships.

Loop:

The adaptive mechanism defining evaluation, retry, repair, recovery, escalation and exit behavior.

Harness:

A governed engineering execution contract containing Graph, Loops, Agents, Skills, Tools, Models, Context, Policies, Permissions, Environment, Limits and Evidence requirements.

Pipeline:

A lifecycle composition of Harnesses.

Policy:

A governance rule determining what is allowed, required or prohibited.

Context:

The relevant information supplied to an Agent for an engineering task.

Evidence:

Immutable proof of what happened during engineering execution.

Engineering State:

The continuously maintained understanding of the application.

